}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D-RECQ (recomputed): WRN is the only MSI-selective RecQ helicase
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The RecQ-family comparison (Achilles CRISPR-CERES, all lineages, the
// recorded artifact's cohort: 32 MSI / 413 MSS). The kernel
// recomputes WRN's MSI-vs-MSS Wilcoxon here (P = 1.1e-8, median -0.49 vs
// -0.11) and lifts it to the family-uniqueness claim through a Declared
// rule. The other three RecQ helicases (BLM P=0.65, RECQL P=0.58,
// RECQL5 P=0.11) are NON-significant and RECQL4 is absent from the 18Q4
// CERES matrix — their non-selectivity is a Declared scientific judgment,
// NOT a derived warrant: a null cannot be derived (you cannot prove "no
// effect" from "failed to find an effect"). So uniqueness composes one
// kernel-derived positive (WRN selective) with the declared interpretation
// of the three kernel-computed n.s. p-values cited in the rule's rationale.

