// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// C-VAL (recomputed): WRN depletion impairs MSI viability (competition assay)
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The wet-lab competition-assay two-way ANOVA (ED Fig 3b, day 10), kernel-
// recomputed via the nested-ANOVA dispatch (stats:Nested SampleSet, value ~
// is_WRN + guide). The two MSI lines KM12 and OVK18 are recomputed (each: 18 sgWRN +
// 12 negative-control day-10 relative-ratio values; the paper's two-way
// ANOVA P = 2.7e-19 / 1.2e-7). Each plan emits stats:lt(mean_diff_of(s), 0)
// (sgWRN mean strictly below control = impaired). A declared bridge composes
// both MSI lines into onco:SelectiveViabilityDependence(WRN, MSI). The MSS
// lines (ES2, SW620) are NON-significant (paper P = 0.37 / 0.23, recomputed
// to Fail) — their "spared" status is the declared judgment (a null is not
// derivable), cited in the bridge rationale. Source data is the pinned Nature
// per-figure XLSX (data/MANIFEST.md); this replaces the linked-external
// va_competition ToolArtifact.

resource wrn:viability_directionality_witness : stats:ImpossibilityWitness {
    reflection:declared_by = "wrn-paper:viability-impairment-directionality";
    reflection:rationale   = "Synthetic lethality predicts WRN depletion IMPAIRS (not enhances) MSI viability: the directional claim is sgWRN viability below negative-control viability (group A mean < group B). The inverse is not the hypothesis, licensing the one-sided test.";
}

