// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// C-MECH (recomputed): WRN depletion causes cell-cycle arrest in MSI
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The downstream DSB-driven-DDR consequence, kernel-recomputed from ED Fig 4b
// (cell-cycle distribution, %S-phase). Three MSI lines — KM12, SW48, OVK18 —
// each: 6 sgWRN (sgWRN2+sgWRN3, 3 reps each) + 3 negative-control (sgCh2-2)
// %S-phase values, nested two-way ANOVA (value ~ is_WRN + guide; the paper's
// design, kernel-recomputed: KM12 P=6.1e-7, SW48 P=3.5e-4, OVK18 P=2.6e-6).
// Group A = sgWRN, Group B = sgCh2-2; the directional claim is sgWRN %S-phase
// strictly below control (arrest reduces the S-phase fraction) ⇒
// stats:lt(mean_diff_of(s), 0). The MSS lines (SW620 P=0.16, SW837 P=0.67,
// ES2 P=0.69) are non-significant (recomputed to Fail; the declared "spared"
// judgment, a null is not derivable), cited in the bridge rationale. Source:
// pinned Nature ED Fig 4 XLSX (data/MANIFEST.md).

resource wrn:cellcycle_directionality_witness : stats:ImpossibilityWitness {
    reflection:declared_by = "wrn-paper:cellcycle-arrest-directionality";
    reflection:rationale   = "DSB-driven cell-cycle arrest reduces the proliferating (S-phase) fraction: the directional claim is sgWRN %S-phase below negative-control %S-phase (group A mean < group B). The inverse (WRN loss increasing S-phase) is not the hypothesis, licensing the one-sided test.";
}

