// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// C-MECH (recomputed): WRN depletion causes apoptosis in MSI
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The other downstream DSB-driven-DDR consequence, kernel-recomputed from ED
// Fig 4c (Annexin-V apoptosis, total apoptotic fraction). Same three MSI lines
// (KM12 P=3.4e-3, SW48 P=3.6e-4, OVK18 P=3.6e-5; nested two-way ANOVA). Here
// the directional claim flips: WRN depletion INCREASES apoptosis, so the
// SampleSet places the negative control first (group A = sgCh2-2) and sgWRN
// second (group B = sgWRN2+sgWRN3), giving mean_a (control) < mean_b (sgWRN)
// ⇒ stats:lt(mean_diff_of(s), 0) when apoptosis rises. The MSS lines (SW620
// P=0.10, SW837 P=0.41, ES2 P=0.57) are non-significant (the declared 'spared'
// judgment). Source: pinned Nature ED Fig 4 XLSX (data/MANIFEST.md).

resource wrn:apoptosis_directionality_witness : stats:ImpossibilityWitness {
    reflection:declared_by = "wrn-paper:apoptosis-induction-directionality";
    reflection:rationale   = "DSB-driven apoptosis raises the apoptotic fraction: the directional claim is negative-control apoptosis below sgWRN apoptosis (group A = control mean < group B = sgWRN mean). The inverse (WRN loss reducing apoptosis) is not the hypothesis, licensing the one-sided test.";
}

