// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// C-MMR (recomputed): restoring MMR partially rescues WRN dependence
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The MMR-restoration causal dissection (ED Fig 10c, relative viability,
// n = 6 biological replicates), kernel-recomputed via the new
// crossed-ANOVA dispatch (stats:Crossed SampleSet, `value ~ CL + guide`, guide CROSSED). The
// HCT116 derivatives: Ch2 (MMR-deficient, ∗), Ch3+5+sgCh2-2 (MMR-restored, †),
// Ch3+5+sgMLH1-1 (MLH1 re-knocked-out, ‡), Ch3+5+sgMLH1-2 (§). Each contrast
// is a pair of derivatives × the shWRN guides (shWRN1, shWRN2, 6 reps each),
// two-way ANOVA testing the CL (MMR-context) main effect on relative viability.
// Three contrasts reproduce the paper EXACTLY (recompute-findings F3):
//   ∗ vs † (restore MMR)        P = 5.7e-20  → restoration rescues
//   † vs ‡ (MLH1-KO #1)         P = 3.3e-12  → re-sensitizes (MMR-attributable)
//   † vs § (MLH1-KO #2)         P = 1.6e-16  → re-sensitizes (MMR-attributable)
// Each SampleSet places the lower-viability (MMR-deficient / re-deficient) arm
// as group A, so the directional claim is stats:lt(mean_diff_of(s), 0): the
// MMR-deficient context sustains LOWER WRN-depletion viability than the
// MMR-restored context. The rescue establishes restoration helps; the two
// MLH1-KO re-sensitization controls establish the rescue is attributable to MMR
// (not the chromosome transfer). "Partially" — the rescue is modest (Ch3+5
// shWRN viability ≈0.71, not back to 1.0) — is the declared qualifier carried
// in the bridge rationale. This replaces the linked-external mmr_restoration
// ToolArtifact (retired in wrn-phase5). Source: pinned Nature ED Fig 10 XLSX.

resource wrn:mmr_directionality_witness : stats:ImpossibilityWitness {
    reflection:declared_by = "wrn-paper:mmr-restoration-directionality";
    reflection:rationale   = "MMR proficiency sustains WRN-depletion viability: the directional claim is that the MMR-deficient (or MLH1-re-knocked-out) context shows LOWER shWRN viability than the MMR-restored context (group A mean < group B). The inverse (MMR restoration reducing viability) is not the hypothesis, licensing the one-sided test.";
}

// ── ∗ vs † : restoring MMR (Ch2 → Ch3+5+sgCh2-2) rescues shWRN viability ──
